  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: a2b79f2d85f1d9744a163ff045d2e5af, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The fleet garage. Twelve hours behind the wheel and the Volga's clutch is shot again. Can I go?
    midDaysAnswer: My building in the western block. Checked the locks, looters everywhere. Cab won't start, so I walked.
    finalDaysAnswer: Nowhere. The cab's dead in the depot yard. I walked through the ash like everybody else.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My place on the east side. Same route every night, I could drive it blind.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: A fare out to Varka and back. Car ran like a dream, roads wide open the whole way.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: My brother's flat. I've bunked there since the wife left me. No kids, nothing to go home to.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My nose won't stop running. Twelve hours breathing exhaust will do that. That's it. Next question.
    midDaysAnswer: I get dizzy when I stand up too fast. It passes. Don't you write that down.
    finalDaysAnswer: My ears ring. All day, all night. Could be the sirens, could be me. What does it matter?
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Healthy as a horse. Haven't driven in months, so there's no fumes in my lungs.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Two weeks in bed with a fever, doctor's orders. Haven't left the flat once.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nothing. Clean lungs. I gave up the cab years ago. I push papers at the ispolkom now.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Move it along, would you? I have been standing here twelve minutes.
    - You need to check the papers or what? I do not have all day.
    - Someone should sort out the roads into this district. Absolute mess.
    midDays:
    - My cab does not start anymore. Three years I kept that engine running.
    - Half the streets are blocked now. You know that, right? Your people closed them.
    - Do not look at me like that. I am just trying to get home.
    finalDays:
    - Go ahead, take your time. Not like the world is ending or anything.
    - I have nowhere to drive and nowhere to be. Happy now?
    - You are still stamping papers. Fine. Stamp the paper. I will wait.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
